  "schema": 1,
  "title": "Confirmatory comparisons behind docs/model-guide.md (2026-10 eval runs)",
  "notes": [
    "Written from the guide's recommendations, before re-running any statistics on the stored results.",
    "One family per decision the guide makes. Holm is applied within each family; the report also shows Holm across every family (the guide as a whole) and BH within the family.",
    "A comparison names its runs by run dir; a list of run dirs is a seed group, compared on the per-item mean pass over seeds.",
    "direction: 'a>b' or 'a<b' (on the metric's own scale; for mae lower is better) uses a two-sided test and counts as confirmed only if the adjusted p < alpha and the estimate has the declared sign. 'equivalent' is a TOST within +/- margin.",
    "Margins are fixed a priori: 0.10 (10 percentage points) for accuracy and refusal rates, the smallest gap that would change a model choice on 100-item subsets; 0.5 CVSS points for MAE.",
    "Descriptive single-model statements in the guide (for example 'hermes never refused', 'vision 79% complied') are not comparisons and are not in any family.",
    "Amended 2026-10-11 (round 2, see the stats AMENDMENTS log): each comparison now has a declared primary analysis (defaults.primary: the PROTOCOL C1.4 exclusions has_signal / no_leak / no_frr_exclude, errors as fail, CVSS items without a parsed prediction imputed at the constant-7.5 baseline error) and pre-registered sensitivity analyses (defaults.sensitivity) that can downgrade a verdict. D1 is an intersection-union family ('best of k'). This round-1 plan is post hoc by construction: its runs are development runs, so the report labels it exploratory.",
    "Amended 2026-10-11 (round 4): a declared exclusion whose flag is missing on any item makes a comparison not evaluable, so the exclusions are now declared per suite where the flag exists (has_signal on nvd-cwe and ctibench-vsp, frr_exclude on cse-frr, no_leak everywhere) instead of as plan-wide defaults. Same exclusions in effect as before; no result was consulted."
  ],
